🚀 Hands-on Project: Kubernetes Headless Service 🚀

(*) What we'll build

                    Kubernetes Cluster
                           │
                    Headless Service
                    db-headless
                    ClusterIP: None
                           │
             ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
             │             │             │
          mysql-0       mysql-1       mysql-2
          10.x.x.x      10.x.x.x      10.x.x.x
             │             │             │
             └─────────────┴─────────────┘
                    Individual Pods

The important difference:
  - Normal Service : client → service → one of the Pods
  - Headless Service : client → DNS → Pod IPs directly

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(*) Phase 1 — Create namespace
namespace.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: headless-ns

# kubectl apply -f namespace.yaml

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(*) Phase 2 — Create Headless Service
headless-svc.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: headless-svc
  namespace: headless-ns
spec:
  clusterIP: None
  selector:
    app: database-app
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 3306
      targetPort: 3306

# kubectl apply -f headless-svc.yaml

# kubectl get svc -n headless-ns                                                                                                                   
NAME           TYPE        CLUSTER-IP   EXTERNAL-IP   PORT(S)    AGE
headless-svc   ClusterIP   None         <none>        3306/TCP   21m

🔥 Important
Here,
clusterIP: None
That's what makes this service headless. There is no virtual ClusterIP.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(*) Phase 3 — Create StatefulSet
database.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: StatefulSet
metadata:
  name: database
  namespace: headless-ns
spec:
  serviceName: headless-svc
  replicas: 3

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: database-app

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: database-app

    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx:alpine
          ports:
            - containerPort: 3306

# kubectl apply -f database.yaml

# kubectl get pods -n headless-ns -o wide                                                                                                           
NAME         READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE   IP             NODE       NOMINATED NODE   READINESS GATES
database-0   1/1     Running   0          24m   10.244.0.214   minikube   <none>           <none>
database-1   1/1     Running   0          24m   10.244.0.215   minikube   <none>           <none>
database-2   1/1     Running   0          24m   10.244.0.216   minikube   <none>           <none> 

Notice something very important: database-0, database-1, database-2
